diagnosis_text:
The outage is not the WAN uplink or R1. IP reachability to the “Internet” is fine: PC1 can ping outside IPs (e.g., 203.0.113.1/.5), R1 can ping its ISP neighbor (203.0.113.1), and the core to R1 links are up. The failure users see is DNS resolution. PC1 is configured to use 10.5.0.4 as DNS (srv1). Queries to it are refused with “recursion not available” (nslookup from PC1 shows REFUSED). On srv1, BIND is running and its configuration explicitly disables recursion and only serves an internal authoritative zone: named.conf contains “recursion no; … zone ‘jeremysitlab.com’ { type master; }”. Therefore, any lookup for external names (www.example.com, etc.) fails even though the network path is working, making browsers “tim
